==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gory|Gories]] spawn, delay 13.33~26.67 seconds<sup>400f~800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Baa Baa]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 6.67~20 seconds<sup>200f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 20~33.33 seconds<sup>600f~1,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 90% HP:
**Infinite [[Celeboodle]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
**4 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 0.07~0.67 seconds<sup>2f~20f</sup>.
**4 [[Celeboodle]]s spawn, delay 0.07~0.13 seconds<sup>2f~4f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Just about any attackers will work against the Celeboodles, due to their low range and [[Single Attack]]. Be sure to shield them with a steady line of meatshields, for the Celeboodles hit hard. [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Sexy Legs Cat]] and [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] are competent ranged attackers that can easily whittle down their health, provided you defend them properly. Area Attackers are even better for this stage, as they are able to hit several of the Celeboodles at once. If you happen to own [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]], this stage will prove quite easy.

